# Exact cached post-live --all findings; answers explain only the anchors of their class.

[sliver] These 1.566 by 27.590 mm lands are the complete source cover's upper retaining-lip bearing faces in its baked RX -50° manufacturing pose. They span native S 10.45–38.04 at N 6.30 and belong to the full relaxed broad-wall snap, not an isolated rigid catch. The complete 4372-facet source is retained; the 0.30 mm end air / 0.48 mm bearing air /1.20 mm engagement are referenced against the complete host groove. New reference fit force/life is unmeasured.
alternatives: Thicker or wider lips require changed groove/air datums and a new snap-force/fit evaluation. Shortening the lip or making a chopped catch changes the engaged span and the full spring action. An externally latched cover eliminates this lip bearing while replacing the source snap mechanism.
