[ceiling] This is the complete source cover's 1.30 mm bezel above its 20.50 by 40.50 mm display window, in the baked RX -50° manufacturing pose. The flat underside is CAD Z 17.75. Current native first bezel roof is nozzle Z 17.96 with 197 Bridge and 116 Overhang-wall deposits, 0.24 mm model step/Bridge HEIGHT; support-interface highest Z 17.24 gives 0.48 mm nominal separation to underside 17.72. Tree (auto) supports actually emit for this object. The complete source wall/lip span is preserved; physical removal and this reference print are unrecorded.
alternatives: Growing the bezel outward to 1.60 or 2.00 mm retains its inner snap datums with more stock but changes the authentic bezel section/thermal exposure. Printing the bezel toward the bed changes the production orientation being represented. A separate bedded face plate removes this ceiling while adding another joint and changing the full source cover.
