[thin] These minima are local curved lower-wall/root stock of the intact relaxed source cover, approximately 1.246 mm at the cached positions; they are not a uniform wall-thickness specification. The whole 29.80 by 49.75 mm cover and both long retaining lips remain intact to represent its broad-wall elastic engagement. The identified full-cover physical evidence has limited fit/removal scope; these current reference bytes are unprinted and provide no force/lifetime acceptance.
alternatives: Thickening the sidewalls can add stock but changes their flexural stiffness and needs a longer span or revised relief plus a new fit/force evaluation. Shortening to a thicker isolated catch changes the spring/engagement mechanism. A rigid two-piece cover avoids these flexures while no longer representing the source snap.
